Title: The  Molly Brown House Museum in Denver, Colorado
Physical description: 1 photograph : digital, tiff file, color.

Notes: The house was the home of American philanthropist, socialite, and activist Margaret "Molly" Brown, who was known as "The Unsinkable Molly Brown" because she survived the sinking of the RMS "Titanic" in 1912. The house was built in the 1880s by architect William A. Lang.;
